1
00:00:00,069 --> 00:00:06,444
One disputed invoice can begin with a simple question: is this the right company?

2
00:00:06,907 --> 00:00:10,078
Veyra turns that question into an evidence case.

3
00:00:10,181 --> 00:00:15,092
It keeps the request, source, timestamp and confidence together,

4
00:00:15,127 --> 00:00:19,040
so a reviewer can see what is known, what remains uncertain,

5
00:00:19,075 --> 00:00:23,023
and why. The live demonstration is a French company lookup.

6
00:00:23,092 --> 00:00:29,525
A visitor enters SIREN 632012100 and sees a quote before paying:

7
00:00:29,605 --> 00:00:35,167
zero point zero zero five USDC on Base.

8
00:00:35,689 --> 00:00:39,730
The visitor approves the exact amount from their own wallet.

9
00:00:39,926 --> 00:00:42,238
Veyra never receives the wallet key.

10
00:00:42,422 --> 00:00:47,567
Sirenic returns the company profile for L’Oréal, with active registry status.

11
00:00:47,693 --> 00:00:54,880
Veyra verifies the provider’s Ed25519 response signature in the browser,

12
00:00:54,915 --> 00:00:58,376
and links the result to the public verification receipt.

13
00:00:58,793 --> 00:01:01,429
Payment is a separate fact.

14
00:01:01,683 --> 00:01:09,045
Base confirms the transaction succeeded in block 57,501,654:

15
00:01:09,171 --> 00:01:17,265
precisely 0.005 USDC to the quoted recipient.

16
00:01:17,681 --> 00:01:21,340
The signature proves the response came from the provider.

17
00:01:21,467 --> 00:01:24,393
The Base receipt proves that payment settled.

18
00:01:24,555 --> 00:01:29,965
Neither proves bank account ownership, payment instructions, sanctions status,

19
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,914
or solvency. A person still makes the decision.

20
00:01:34,075 --> 00:01:39,858
Other scenarios are clearly marked synthetic; shipment data is test mode.

21
00:01:40,159 --> 00:01:46,371
Veyra. Evidence for decisions. Human judgement stays in control.
